                "favorite_count": 354,
                "geo_lat": null,
                "geo_lon": null,
                "id": "1955034918192321001",
                "in_reply_to_post_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_username": null,
                "place_country_code": null,
                "place_country_name": null,
                "place_full_name": null,
                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "quote",
                "quote_count": 9,
                "quoted_status_id": "1954963775813271941",
                "quoted_status_profile_id": "1192549822865297409",
                "quoted_status_profile_username": "GovAndyBeshear",
                "reply_count": 152,
                "retweet_count": 118,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": ".@GovAndyBeshear, enough with the fear mongering. Here\u2019s the truth about how the One, Big, Beautiful Bill will strengthen Medicaid for Kentucky\u2019s most vulnerable. \u2b07\ufe0f\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f The \u201ccoverage loss\u201d you cite stems from the state\u2019s provider tax payments. The state made a commitment to fund 10% of Medicaid \u2013 the federal government will continue to cover our 90%, and actually increase funding. The federal government will continue to honor our commitment.\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f Our bill does nothing to impact Medicaid benefits for mothers and children.\n\n\u27a1\ufe0f The people who will lose access to Medicaid under our bill are able-bodied individuals who choose not to work, or are already ineligible to receive benefits under the program. This plan is simply the elimination of waste, fraud, and abuse in Medicaid. \n\n\u27a1\ufe0f You claim that 35 rural Kentucky hospitals will close as a result of our bill. Last week, I visited several rural hospitals in my district that you claim will close because of our bill. Every single one of them has said they will stay open providing care to Kentuckians.\n\nAgain, enough with the attempts to scare people. Being a leader means making responsible decisions for taxpayers and the most vulnerable in our Commonwealth. Our bill does exactly that.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": [
                    "GovAndyBeshear"
                ],
                "text_tagged_users_ids": [
                    "1192549822865297409"
                ],
